From 5acf08628269da1ae53490bc3d2b9a7b500bf6e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:25:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/51] fix: post-read / pre-write checks do the paper's tail
 check; RO switch (record deallocation) notifies
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The artifact tested the change notification without bringing the replica up to the shared log tail, so an
event another host had appended but this host had not replayed was missed. Paper §3.3/§3.4.5: the post-read
check 'checks if there were any log updates concerning A', and the writer, after taking the lock bit, 'checks
if there were any log updates since it initially got the index entry'. With DYN_WMETA both checks now sync to
the completed tail first (CheckNotificationResetSynced). The RO switch (CheckSwitchWmetaArray(-1) and
SwitchToReadOnlyByWmeta) now answers with the entry (old wmeta + the key's cn) instead of an empty one, so the
replay notifies and flushes the object as the paper's deallocation event requires (was cn -1: neither).

Evidence: G-B attempts 9-11 (torn reads: an RO-path read overlapped a remote RO->RW promotion + write that the
reader's replica had not replayed; stale-record writes after a remote RO switch).
NR tests: scr wmeta-rev 12/12, wmeta-rev 12/12, scr 9/9, none 9/9 (new: ro_switch_notifies_on_replay_...).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
